    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Saka were the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a>, Iranian-speaking horse nomads spread from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aral-sea">Aral Sea</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altai-mountains">Altai</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a>.</li><li>They formed many tribes rather than one state, fighting and serving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and resisting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a>.</li><li>Driven south by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuezhi">Yuezhi</a> in the 2nd century BCE, they founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-scythians">Indo-Scythian kingdoms</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pazyryk-burials">Pazyryk</a> tombs in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altai-mountains">Altai</a>, linked to the wider Saka-Scythian world, filled with ice soon after burial and so preserved the oldest known knotted pile carpet.</p></aside>
    </section>

